`Chats` screen is `conversations` feature. It just displays as `Chats`.

# Purpose

This document defines how Relay loads, renders, and synchronizes the user's conversation list in the Expo application.

The primary goal is to provide an offline-first, local-first experience where conversations are displayed immediately from the local database and synchronized with the server in the background.

---

# High Level Architecture

                   Chats
                     │
                     ▼
                 Local DB
                     │
                     ▼
             Render Chats
                     │
                     │
                background
                     │
                     ▼
                Sync Server
                     │
                     ▼
            GET /conversations
                     │
                     ▼
                latest data
                     │
                     ▼
                Update Local DB
                     │
                     ▼
               UI re-renders

---

# Local-First Rendering

Local DB is the local source of truth for the currently rendered conversation data.

When the user opens the Chats screen:

Chats Screen
↓
Conversations Repository
↓
Local DB
↓
Conversations data
↓
Render UI

If the device is offline, previously synchronized conversations should still be displayed.

The user should not see a blocking:

Loading conversations...

when local conversation data is already available.

---

# Background Synchronization

After the Chats screen has rendered local data, Relay synchronizes conversation data with the backend.

Local DB Render
↓
Background Sync
↓
GET /conversations
↓
Server
↓
Conversations data
↓
Local DB

The synchronization process should update:

Conversations
Conversation participants
Users profile information
Last message information
Unread state
Conversation timestamps

The synchronization process must not block the initial rendering of the Chats screen.

---

# Chats UI Data

A Chats list item should contain all information required to render a conversation without making another network request.

Conceptually:

type ChatListItem = {
conversationId: string;
serverId: string;

user: {
id: string;
displayName: string;
username: string;
avatarUrl: string | null;
};

lastMessage: {
id: string;
preview: string;
createdAt: string;
} | null;

unreadCount: number;
};

---

# Chats UI

For a direct conversation, the Chats screen should display:

Chats

[DP] user 1 10:42 AM
last message 2 (unread count)

[DP] user 2 Yesterday
last message

Each direct conversation row contains:

User avatar
User display name
Last message preview
Last message timestamp
Unread count

`User` means here conversation's other user from currently logged in user.

---

# Conversation Ordering

The Chats screen should display conversations in descending order of the latest message.

last_message_at DESC

